Hi!

Especially for that I bought the DiNovo a few months ago.
At the University I work with a Bluetooth Analyzer (FTS) but at that point
i was not able to decrypt the data (between Mediapad and PC) because the
Logitech driver
always generated new PIN codes while pairing and at that time it was not
possible to re-enter the
PIN into the Analyzer after starting it to Sync. It is essential to have the
Analyzer watch the pairing
process and get the pin to reconstruct the appropriate Link-Key.

A few days ago I installed an update of FTS and now it is possible to
re-enter the PIN-code but
unfortunately I sold the DiNovo because without the option of using the
display for my
own purposes it has been useless for me.

Heiko



